{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1s5:000001:issue_created:sase-1s5:dd4dca3f6ba77a05d208348c011d16aaacd836567429f940d913f2887e62474b","timestamp":"2026-11-08T11:51:27Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.cy--6","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-1s5","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-1s5","title":"Health-watch fixes: wait notices name their waiter, failed staged-monitor sessions never park waiters silently, fleet snapshots build within their refresh timeout, and dismissed runs converge in the published agents sidecar","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-08T11:51:27Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.cy--6","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:51:27Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"Every \"Wait dependency can never self-resolve\" notice names the blocked agent (never a project key). An agent waiting on a session whose root turn and monitor both failed is flagged within one wait_checks pass instead of waiting silently. apollo's presentation fleet snapshot builds in well under the gateway's 4 s refresh timeout, so remote fleet readers stop receiving stale \"timeout\" snapshots every minute. agent_state_refresh finds each run's dismissed bundle by exact identity, so dismissed runs stop being published as active or waiting forever, and an incomplete dismissal lookup is never reported as live.","design":"plan:202611/health_watch_fixes.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202611/health_watch_fixes.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
